# Legion Archive: plaintext Discord exports are internal-only and must never
# be committed (public repo). Only sealed ciphertext ships — see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-legion-archive-design.md
archive-export*/
public/archive/
public/archive-e2e/
e2e/.archive/
public/accolades/
public/rank-requirements/
src/data/accolades/
src/data/rank-requirements/
legacy-accolades*.json
error_reports/

# Deathwatch tracker: real names live only in the server's database. The Manage pages' "Download backup" file (the
# old site made one with the same name), the old site's data, rolling backups and config, and the .7z archives it
# came in must never be committed. scripts/archive-leak-guard.mjs refuses them too, ignored or not.
deathwatch-backup*.json
deathwatch-data*.json
data-backup/
config.php
*.7z

# The guild's member list: the server asks Discord for it live. A copy must never be committed
# (scripts/archive-leak-guard.mjs refuses it too, ignored or not).
discord-members*.json

# Test tooling output
coverage/
.stryker-tmp/
reports/

# New development notes (specs, plans, handoffs, ideas) stay on the maintainers' machines.
# Files already tracked in these folders stay tracked.
docs/superpowers/
docs/handoff/
docs/ideas/

# A local export of the guild's roles
roles_list.txt
